 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Closedness and disjointness of the four boundary loci",
 "statement": "The subschemes $Z_i$ are closed in $U$. Each $Z_{i,k}$ is closed in\n$V_i$, their underlying closed sets are disjoint, and $\\psi_i$ is an\nisomorphism over an open neighbourhood of $Z_i$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-prop-nagata-sketch-prepared/lemma-nagata-boundary-loci.md",
  "place": "node lemma-nagata-boundary-loci, order 267"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-nagata-two-open-boundary-loci",
  "def-nagata-two-open-graph-extensions"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Since the support of $Z_i$ is $U\\setminus U_j$, it is closed in $U$ and\ncontained in $U_i$. Base change of this closed immersion along $\\psi_i$\ngives each closed immersion $Z_{i,k}\\hookrightarrow V_i$. The supports of\n$Z_i$ and $Z_j$ are disjoint because\n$(U\\setminus U_j)\\cap(U\\setminus U_i)=U\\setminus(U_i\\cup U_j)=\\varnothing$;\ntheir inverse images in $V_i$ are consequently disjoint. Finally,\n$Z_i\\subseteq U_i$, and [lemma-nagata-graph-extension] identifies\n$\\psi_i^{-1}(U_i)\\to U_i$ with an isomorphism. This gives the required\nisomorphism on the open neighbourhood $U_i$ of $Z_i$.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-graph-extension"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
  "lemma-nagata-graph-extension"
 ],
